# Citation File Format 1.2.0 — https://citation-file-format.github.io/
#
# GitHub reads this file and renders a "Cite this repository" button, and Zenodo,
# Software Heritage and several reference managers parse it directly. It is the
# machine-readable twin of the Citation section in README.md: if one changes,
# change the other.
#
# `preferred-citation` points at the MA-IDM paper because that is the work a
# reader of this simulator should cite first; the dynamic-regression paper and
# the two foundational papers follow under `references`.

cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this simulator in your work, please cite the underlying papers
  listed below rather than the software alone.
title: "traffic-sim: an interactive ring-road simulator for stochastic car-following models"
abstract: >-
  A dependency-free browser simulator of the Intelligent Driver Model on a
  one-lane ring road, with three interchangeable stochastic driver-noise models —
  a Gaussian process (MA-IDM), an autoregressive AR(p) process
  (dynamic-regression IDM) and i.i.d. white noise (B-IDM) — drawn from published
  Bayesian car-following calibration research. It shows how the temporal
  correlation of the acceleration residual, not only its variance, governs the
  formation of stop-and-go waves in the absence of any bottleneck.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Chengyuan
    email: enzozcy@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-8463-7380"
    affiliation: "Department of Civil Engineering, McGill University, Montreal, Canada"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Chengyuan-Zhang/traffic-sim"
url: "https://chengyuan-zhang.github.io/traffic-sim/"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - traffic simulation
  - microscopic traffic simulation
  - intelligent driver model
  - IDM
  - car-following model
  - stochastic car-following
  - Bayesian calibration
  - Gaussian process
  - autoregressive model
  - ring road
  - stop-and-go waves
  - phantom traffic jam
  - traffic flow theory
  - fundamental diagram
  - MA-IDM

